Interestingly enough, having just typed up that last post, it's gotten me
thinking...

I've just taken delivery of a lot of old PC bits & disks. Mostly 18Gb SCSI
drives. So I've built up 2 boxes with 8 disks in each. Only old Xeon 500
processors, but all good stuff in its day.

Now I'm thinking that what I have is effectively 2 x 100GB disk arrays...
Consuming (lets say) 8W per disk, thats nearly 130W worth of energy plus
the processors, etc.

I think that in the long-run, I'd be better off just spending 100 quid on
a couple of 120GB drive and be done with it... Not as much fun though!

Oh how technology moves on!

